		(property "Description" "TI TPS62933F 3.8-30V in, 3A synchronous buck, FORCED-PWM (FCCM -- fixed switching frequency even at light load, per datasheet section 9.3.8), RT pin to GND selects 1.2MHz (min 1.0MHz per EC table) -- satisfies Realtek RTL8125B reference V122 notice: '3.3V from switching regulator must be PWM mode and Freq>=1Mhz' (main-rail TPS565201 is ~580kHz Eco pulse-skipping, non-compliant, hence this dedicated +3V3_ETH rail; Fix 4, decision trail in task-10-report.md Fix pass + docs/sourcing.md). SS pin: >=6.8nF required, 10nF -> ~1.45ms soft start. BST-SW 100nF. FB ref 0.8V, divider 31.6k/10k -> 3.328V. Candidates honestly rejected from live datasheets: TPS54308 (350kHz FCCM), SY8120B1 (500kHz), SY8120I (500kHz), SY8201 (500kHz), TPS562231 (850kHz Eco), TPS562242 (1.4MHz but Eco pulse-skip), LMR33620A/B (400kHz / auto-PFM), MT2494 (no LCSC listing), SCT2330 (400kHz PSM), RT6253B (forced PWM but 580kHz). Sourced: LCSC C5219272 (923-1,235 stock observed, $1.11@1, live-checked 2026-07-15)." (at 0 0 0) (hide yes) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
		(property "ki_keywords" "buck converter step-down 3.3V forced PWM FCCM 1.2MHz" (at 0 0 0) (hide yes) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
